{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Revise Test Cases (Created)",
  "description": "When FINAL_TEST_CASES_*_UPDATED.md is first created (renamed from _PENDING or _OK), trigger test case revision",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileCreated",
    "patterns": [
      "**/2_Validator/FINAL_TEST_CASES_*_UPDATED.md"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are acting as the QA-Validator-Agent. Read the feedback notes at the top of the edited FINAL_TEST_CASES_*_UPDATED.md file in the 2_Validator/ folder or any change in the file. Also read the test_plan_OK.md, logic_explanation.md, AND manual_input.md (or manual_input_OK.md) from 1_Expert/ for full context — manual_input.md contains human observations and clarifications that OVERRIDE AI-generated content (treat filled-in answers and notes as mandatory inputs). Read the @TestCasesDesign.md steering file for formatting standards. Use the @ContextIntegrator.md skill to ensure human feedback overrides AI logic. Use the @TestCaseStandardizer.md skill to rewrite all test cases into the exact format required by @TestCasesDesign.md. Follow @context_efficiency.md rules.\n\nRELATED TICKET ANALYSIS (runs before test case generation):\nIf manual_input.md contains reference tickets (Jira URLs or keys like POS-XXXX, OP-XXXX):\n1. Fetch each related ticket via Jira MCP (get summary, description, acceptance criteria)\n2. Assess impact — does the related ticket reveal:\n   - New test scenarios NOT covered by the current test plan?\n   - Clarifications about feature behavior (e.g., flag scope, sync mechanism)?\n   - Constraints that should appear in preconditions?\n3. If impactful (new scenarios or behavioral clarifications):\n   - Update 1_Expert/logic_explanation.md — ONLY the 'Linked Ticket Analysis' table section. Append rows with: Ticket | Relevance | Status | Key Findings. Do NOT modify any other section of logic_explanation.md.\n   - Incorporate new scenarios into the test cases output.\n4. If purely contextual (no new test scenarios needed): Update logic_explanation.md Linked Ticket Analysis only.\n5. If the ticket was already analyzed (row exists in the table), SKIP it.\n\nIMPORTANT — Output rules:\n- Extract the ticket ID from the _UPDATED.md filename.\n- Write the revised output to FINAL_TEST_CASES_[TicketID]_PENDING.md in the SAME 2_Validator/ folder.\n- If FINAL_TEST_CASES_[TicketID]_PENDING.md already exists, OVERWRITE it. Do NOT create a second file or append a number.\n- The snapshot hook will automatically back up the file before overwrite.\n- Use a single fsWrite call to write the complete file content in one operation — do NOT split across fsWrite + fsAppend.\n- After writing _PENDING.md, DELETE the _UPDATED.md file. Suffixes represent lifecycle state — the file transitions from _UPDATED → _PENDING, it is NOT a new file alongside the old one.\n\nMANDATORY POST-REVISION INTEGRITY CHECK (from @qa-validator-workflow.md): Before writing output, verify: (1) Count all TCs in source vs output — missing TCs not explicitly removed by feedback MUST be re-added with full content; (2) TC IDs are sequential with NO gaps — renumber if TCs were removed; (3) Every TC has ALL required sections (header, Priority, Test Type, Automation Status, Regression Potential, Regression Candidate, Source, Preconditions, Test Steps with Expected per step, Expected Result, Test Data); (4) Test Summary Matrix rows match detailed TC sections 1:1 — same count, same IDs, same titles; (5) Add a revision comment block at top documenting what was removed/added/modified and before/after TC count. If a TC cannot be recovered, flag with <!-- MISSING --> comment.\n\n⚠️ CRITICAL: Output filename is ALWAYS FINAL_TEST_CASES_[TicketID]_PENDING.md. If it already exists, OVERWRITE it. Never create duplicates.\n\nWrite to 2_Validator/ (test cases) and 1_Expert/logic_explanation.md (Linked Ticket Analysis section only). Stop."
  }
}
